closed	p3	CORS-on-500 masking: unhandled 500s in dev reach the client as a transport failure, not a real error. Starlette ServerErrorMiddleware (always outermost) emits the 500 response OUTSIDE CORSMiddleware, so it ships without Access-Control-Allow-Origin. Cross-origin dev (frontend :5173 -> backend :8000) => browser blocks the response, fetch() rejects with TypeError => api.ts toasts error_network_unreachable and tournament-actions.ts adds tournament_action_reverted + rolls back, hiding the actual server exception. This is what masked the ReopenTournament winner=null 500 (see #262) as a network error and wasted debugging time. Dev-only (prod is same-origin via nginx; a 500 surfaces as a real 500 -> ApiError). Fix: make CORS headers apply to the error-handler response — e.g. a custom 500/exception handler that sets CORS headers, or restructure so CORSMiddleware wraps ServerErrorMiddleware (FastAPI/Starlette do not allow this via add_middleware ordering since ServerErrorMiddleware is forced outermost, so likely a custom handler). Diagnostic/observability only, no user-facing behaviour change in prod. relates:#262
