closed	p2	First-party login endpoints mint tokens for soft-deleted accounts (same class as the refresh-vector fix, which only closed resolution+refresh). An IC-manually-deleted account keeps its auth_method rows (soft_delete_user sets only user.deleted_at; auth methods are NOT removed — unlike merge, which reassigns them via reassign_auth_methods), so it can log back in fresh and get new 7d tokens. Unchecked login mints: passkey_login_verify (passkeys.py:412 create_access_token off auth_method.user_uid), discord_callback LOGIN/SIGNUP mode (discord.py existing_auth branch), email/password login + magic-link verify (routes/auth/magic_link.py, _tokens or password path). Fix: resolve the user and reject deleted_at before create_access_token in each login path (or a shared helper). Note: IC-delete refuses VEKN members ('mark deceased instead'), and merge-tombstoned accounts have no surviving auth methods, so the exposed set is non-VEKN IC-deleted accounts with a passkey/discord/email still attached. Lower severity than the refresh vector (needs a surviving credential) but same 'deleted users keep authenticating' goal. Deferred out of the refresh-vector commit per scope. relates:#369
