closed	p2	VEKN event-scan termination conflates absent with transient: fetch_all_events (backend/src/vekn_api.py) counts fetch_event()==None toward the empty-run limit, but fetch_event returns None for BOTH a genuine 404 (no event) AND a swallowed 5xx/ClientError (:438). So a sustained vekn.net outage across ~200 consecutive IDs inside the populated range ends the probe-until-dry scan early and silently skips every event above that point (daily retry recovers the common case, but a persistent partial outage loses data). Fix: have fetch_event signal transient failure distinctly (e.g. raise, or a sentinel) so only 'API confirmed no event' (404/empty/code!=200) advances consecutive_empty; transient errors must NOT count. Note fetch_event has other callers (search_players path etc.) — keep their None-on-error contract or update them. Follow-up to the probe-until-dry fix; the post-loop termination log added there makes premature stops detectable meanwhile. relates:#357
closed	p2	Discord OAuth link/merge flow writes ARCHON_USER_FIELDS members without local_modifications tracking (sibling of the update_user nickname-revert bug, surfaced by that ticket's parity audit): backend/src/routes/auth/discord.py sets user.discord_id (:247/:291/:328), user.contact_discord (:250/:331) and user.nickname (:253/:334) on link-to-existing-account and email-merge, but never adds them to local_modifications. All three are in the nightly legacy merge's ARCHON_USER_FIELDS, so for a user matched to an old-archon member the 04:00 merge reverts the new-stack Discord-linked values: contact_discord/nickname (auto-filled only when empty) get set back to old archon's value or cleared to None; discord_id reverts if the linked Discord differs from old archon's. Fresh Discord-only signups (vekn-less, :341) are unmatched by the merge, so unaffected. Design nuance to settle before fixing: a discord_id from a fresh new-stack OAuth link is authoritative and should pin (track it); contact_discord/nickname are soft auto-fills — decide whether a Discord-derived value should pin against the merge or stay merge-owned. Fix: add local_modifications tracking for whichever fields are chosen to pin, mirroring PATCH /auth/me. Live-run relevant only while the legacy merge runs (until Phase 2).
