closed	p2	Deck text-parse drops X-named crypt cards: try_count_first (engine/src/deck.rs) skipped the count→name separator by greedily consuming any run of x/X/*/space, so a count-prefixed name starting with 'x' lost its leading letter ("1x Xaviar" -> "aviar" -> no match). Since real decklists always carry a count, NO X-named crypt card (Xaviar, Xendil Charmer, Xeper, Xian Quan, Ximena, Xipe Totec) could be text-imported. Fix: treat an x/X run as a multiplier marker only when whitespace follows it (matching krcg's '(x|X)+\\s'); '*' stays unconditional. Found during the krcg card-name-resolution investigation (epic #476).
